Commands worth keeping nearby
These are particularly useful for manually finding missed points:

Accounts
getent passwd
awk -F: '$3 == 0 {print $1,$3}' /etc/passwd
getent group sudo
getent group adm
getent group lpadmin
sudo visudo -c


Password security
sudo awk -F: '$2 == "" {print $1}' /etc/shadow
sudo chage -l hhogan
sudo chage -l bbanner


Firewall and SSH
sudo ufw status numbered
sudo ufw status verbose
sudo sshd -t
sudo systemctl status ssh


Services and ports
systemctl --type=service --state=running
sudo ss -tulpn
systemctl list-timers --all


Installed applications
dpkg -l | grep -Ei 'nmap|zenmap|ophcrack|john|hydra|wireshark|tshark|nikto|netcat|metasploit'


Files
sudo find /home /tmp /opt /mnt /media -type f \
\( -iname '*.mp3' -o -iname '*.mp4' -o -iname '*.mkv' -o -iname '*.wav' \) -print
